From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:07:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-panther: pull up the touch
 interrupt

Google's panther touch file sets a pull-up on the FT3658's interrupt
pin, gpa7-0 (&ts_irq in gs201-panther-touch.dtsi, EXYNOS_PIN_PULL_UP),
and the Pixel 7's live device tree has it (ts-irq, samsung,pin-pud = 3).
The shared gs201 group has no pull, as the Pixel 7 Pro wants, so
override it in this board file only. Touch worked without it, since the
controller drives the line; this matches stock.

Tested on a Pixel 7 from slot B (7.3.0-rc6), together with the next
patch: the live device tree has samsung,pin-pud = 3 in ts-irq-pins,
pinctrl reports gpa7-0 in that group, and the controller probes (chip
id 0x56, firmware 0x16) and reports touches across the panel.

Suggested-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
index 8c42276bf..b55b87138 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
@@ -229,6 +229,11 @@ haptics: haptic-driver@43 {
  * Touchscreen: a FocalTech FT3658 on USI0 SPI, wired as the Pixel 7 Pro's
  * S3908 (chip select gpp20-3, interrupt gpa7-0, reset gpp23-2).
  */
+&ts_irq {
+	/* Stock pulls the interrupt line up on this phone, not on the 7 Pro */
+	samsung,pin-pud = <GS101_PIN_PULL_UP>;
+};
+
 &usi0 {
 	samsung,mode = <USI_MODE_SPI>;
 	status = "okay";
